  "synonym_discrimination": null,
  "usage_note": "**Favorite** already means best liked, so **more favorite** and **most favorite** are not standard. *My most favorite* is heard in informal speech but avoided in careful writing, where *my favorite* is enough; *my absolute favorite* and *my all-time favorite* are common ways to add emphasis instead. Standing on its own (*Which is your favorite?*), it is a noun with its own entry: **[[favorite-n|favorite]]** (noun). In British spelling the word is **favourite**, and so is the noun.",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "my most favorite song",
      "correct": "my favorite song",
      "note": "*Most favorite* is heard in informal speech only; careful writing avoids it, because **favorite** already means liked best."
    }
  ],
  "etymology": null,
  "see_also": [
