      "note": "**favorite** standing on its own: *which is your favorite?*"
    }
  ],
  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "Many languages say the one I like most with a superlative; English uses this ordinary adjective before the noun, almost always with a possessive: my favorite, her favorite.",
    "grammar": "**Favorite** comes before a noun (*my favorite song*); on its own it is the noun **favorite** (*this is my favorite*), a separate entry. It is not used with **very**; *most favorite* is heard in informal speech but avoided in careful writing.",
    "culture": null,
    "false_friends": null,
    "pronunciation": "Often said with two syllables, *FAYV-rit*; the full three-syllable form, *FAY-vuh-rit*, is also correct. The stress is on the first syllable either way."
  },
